# CNAME Configuration for Custom Domain
#
# Instructions:
# 1. Rename this file to "CNAME" (without .example extension)
# 2. Replace the domain below with your custom domain
# 3. Configure DNS settings at your domain registrar:
#    - Add a CNAME record pointing to: yourusername.github.io
#    OR
#    - Add A records pointing to GitHub's IPs:
#      185.199.108.153
#      185.199.109.153
#      185.199.110.153
#      185.199.111.153
# 4. Commit and push the CNAME file to your repository
# 5. Wait for DNS propagation (up to 48 hours)
# 6. Enable HTTPS in GitHub Pages settings after DNS is active
#
# Examples:
# www.yourname.com
# yourname.com
# resume.yourname.com

# Uncomment and replace with your domain:
# www.shuvodeepde.com
